**Item 7 — Liquidity (10-K p.25–26)**
- "$2.2 billion of cash and equivalents and $3.5 billion of available committed bank credit … We believe we have a manageable debt maturity profile, with approximately $90 million due February 2027. Furthermore, we have no financial covenants or material adverse change provisions in our bank agreements."
- "We currently expect capital spending for 2026 to be approximately $1.1 billion"; 2026 expected payments: "$378 million of interest on debt, and $418 million under our leasing arrangements."

**Item 7 — Results by region (10-K p.29–31)**
- "Middle East/Asia revenue in 2025 was $5.8 billion, a 4% decrease compared to 2024, resulting from lower activity across multiple product service lines in Saudi Arabia and Malaysia. Partially offsetting these decreases were **improved activity across multiple product service lines in Kuwait**, higher stimulation activity in India, higher drilling related services in Indonesia, and increased fluids services in the United Arab Emirates." (This is the *only* mention of Kuwait in the 10-K — Kuwait is not disclosed separately.)

**Item 1 — Business**
- "In 2025, **91% of our workforce and 85% of management were on local terms** in the countries where they work."
- "No other country accounted for more than 10% of our consolidated revenue" (besides the U.S.); "No other country or single customer accounted for more than 10% of our receivables."
